WEBVTT

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>tsukinuketa aoi sora</b>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>The blue sky has broken through</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>saa dekakeyou</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>Come, let's go out</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>itsumo no namikimichi jitensha wo koideku</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>Riding my bike through the usual avenue</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>ima sugu ni aitai yo</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>"I want to meet you now."</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>omoi ga kaze wo kiri</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>That thought is blown away by the wind,</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>kimi e to hakondeku tegami ni natte</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>and becomes a letter being carried to you</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>koko kara hajimaru monogatari fly!</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>The story that starts from here... Fly!</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>kawariyuku kisetsu ga ashioto wo tatetemo</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>Even if the changing seasons walk on with loud footsteps,</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>sou kawaranai suki to iu tsubasa</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>the wings of love won't change</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>dokomade mo tondeke oozora takaku</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>Fly far away, high into the sky</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.720
<b>koi no tenki yohou hare nochi hare ni nare</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.720
<b>May the weather forecast of love be sunny and clear forever</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>ashita mo asatte mo</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>Tomorrow and the day after tomorrow</b>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.610
<b>Episode 6     A Tiny Resolution</b>

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.950
End of Term 
Examination Results

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.950
Shijou Mitsue

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.910
Saegusa Matsuri

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.620
Pretty impressive.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.710
Anyhow, this is a weight off our shoulders.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.090
Now we have nothing until summer vacation.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.300
Guess so.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.840
We'll need to discuss our plans for summer vacation.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.300
Come to think of it, where's Yurie?

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.730
Hitotsubashi Yurie

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.320
I dropped— I dropped down so far!

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.740
But you don't have to take a makeup exam, do you?

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.370
Just redeem yourself in second term!

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.290
You've been busy with your work as a god this term.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.460
Isn't that kinda your fault?

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.090
What's important is the future!

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.590
And what's right in front of us now is summer vacation!

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:45.560
We have to work hard to make this a beautiful 
summer full of great memories for everyone!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.600
How?

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.060
Come on in to this special pre-summer vacation event!

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.520
Sign: Happy Summer Girls-only Love-Love fortune consultation room

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:57.240
This is Yurie-sama's Happy Summer Girls-only 
Love-Love fortune consultation room!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.490
Line up, line up!

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.490
This is a big hit!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:11.580
So then he asked me if I wanted to 
go on a trip with him this summer—

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.590
What do you think I should do?

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:25.560
When I was in his room, I saw all these 
perverted books hidden under his bed—

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.640
Do all guys like those kind of books?

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.560
I wonder—

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:38.780
For now, please hang this on your wall.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.780
<b>Men are wolves, 
take care</b>

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.200
I don't want such lousy handwriting on my wall!

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:45.910
Matsuri!

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.410
Time for a break.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.960
Well, her handwriting is kinda lousy—

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.940
We're finally doing good business—

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.920
It'd be a shame if we lost all our hard work now.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.510
Let's start the summer with special calligraphy training!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.680
Huh? Special training?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.680
Want me to ask Ken-chan to be your personal tutor?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.610
She'll probably get so nervous her
 writing will end up even worse.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.860
Then do you want to call it quits?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.030
<b>Girls only!!</b>

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.030
<b>Yurie-sama's 
Happy Summer Love-Love 
fortune consultation room</b>

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.030
<b>Yurie-sama's 
Happy Summer Love-Love 
fortune consultation room</b>

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.030
<b>Open for business again!</b>

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.030
There is someone I like.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.500
But it's the first time I've fallen in love with someone.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.710
I don't know what to do!

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.030
You can only fall in love with someone once.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.760
There won't be a second time.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:51.350
What's most important are your feelings.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.350
Talk about lacking experience—

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.350
Mitsue-chan!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.100
So—

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.110
What kind of person is he?

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.150
He's an upperclassman from 2nd year.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.110
From class 2.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.250
Ninomiya Kenji from the calligraphy club.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.720
What do you want!? If you 
don't let me through I'll be late!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.270
Even if it's your turf, cut me some slack!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.900
Please move aside, I'm in a hurry.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.360
Oh well.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.820
Here you go.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.700
Tomorrow I'll bring you some bread.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.330
How wonderful!

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.170
So that's how it happened.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.590
Did that story just now contain the 
reason she fell in love with him?

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.220
How nice—

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.720
So I came here, but—

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.060
he seems to have left to someplace else.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.600
Ninomiya-kun's kinda restless.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.400
It's called active!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.940
Please tell me, god!

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.490
What should I do now?

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.820
How can I hook up with him?

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.410
There's really no need to ask Yurie, 
of all people, for advice on this—

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.620
Mitsue-chan!

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:45.130
Anyway, why not start by trying to figure 
out if what you're feeling is really love?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.840
Do I need to be harassed by a dog again?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.760
Not like that, I mean—

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:57.060
You should think about what to do to 
increase your chances of meeting him.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.230
That's it!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:07.200
But I'm just a young and humdrum first year student—

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.660
I'm in a different grade and class from him.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.370
Then how about joining the calligraphy club he's in?

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.530
Yurie!

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.580
Great idea, god!

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.420
Of course, in a club it won't 
matter if I'm from a different year.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.380
If I get into a club together with him, 
all kind of things could happen—

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.720
I want to do all kinds of fun things!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.140
I'll join the club with you.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.060
I'll join the club as well!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.230
Wouldn't it be awkward if it were just the two of you?

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:44.310
If we go together, I'll be able to give you running advice—

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.070
Gods are—

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.030
Y-Yes?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.530
—such wonderful people!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.330
It's a god's duty to aid those in need!

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.130
Yes, yes that's right.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.130
Gods are great!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.140
Go for it.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.100
I'll do my best—

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.350
Sorry to make you come along.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.180
It's no problem. I'm here for you.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.520
But why the roof?

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.230
It'll be a problem if she enters a club all of a sudden.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.990
Our relationship consultation project did so well—

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:36.280
This is a great opportunity for her, and she'll 
get to work on her handwriting, so it'll be fine.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.240
<b>Calligraphy 
\hClub</b>

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.870
This is the calligraphy club!?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.120
Isn't the clubroom inside the building?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.330
Umm—

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.130
Actually, he's up there because there is no clubroom—

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.670
That's how it is.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.590
So wild—

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.130
Ken-chan!

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.220
Ken-chan!

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.680
He's not there?

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.730
But he left the classroom before us—

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.030
Ninomiya-kun!

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:22.580
Yurie!

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.510
What're you guys doing?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:37.430
<b>Calligraphy 
\hClub</b>

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.430
Sorry about that, it's hot and there's no air-conditioning here—

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.430
So you two are the two new members?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.260
Yes!

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:43.560
Yes.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.640
I'm so glad!

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.520
I've been alone all this time.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.520
Umm—

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.590
It's Kiyomi!

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.440
First year student Noto Kiyomi!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.110
You helped me this morning—

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:56.620
Sorry.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.280
I don't remember at all.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:05.200
Besides calligraphy, I'm not very 
attentive and I have a bad memory.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.170
Anyway, let's try to get along well!

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:08.920
Yes!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.750
Okay!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.170
Er—

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.800
Wait, er—

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:16.760
Hitotsubashi!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:21.680
Yuri-

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.180
-san, isn't it?

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.100
It's "Yurie."

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.290
Ah, sorry.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.560
I really thought I had it this time.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.460
It's okay.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:34.570
You had most of it.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.070
Noto-san and Hitotsubashi-san, huh?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.570
I'm Ninomiya Kenji, second year student!

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.070
We know!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.830
Even though it's almost summer 
vacation, let's do our best!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:44.580
Yes!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.330
Our motto is, "The way of calligraphy it the way of the spirit"!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.160
Isn't this kinda annoying, in many ways?

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.000
I want some refreshment—

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.720
Clear your mind of mundane thoughts,

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.430
and even the fire cools off!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.310
There are insects that eat knotweed,

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.890
there's no accounting for taste!

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.980
If the surroundings change,

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.970
<i>How embarrassing—</i>

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.900
the objects change!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.360
<i>But it's kinda—</i>

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.360
Wait!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.450
Even experts—

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.200
—can make mistakes!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.270
<i>—like that!</i>

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.830
<i>Oh my, what am I thinking!</i>

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.700
There is no cure—

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.410
—for stupidity!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.130
What's up with that yell?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:36.600
It's an attempt to distinguish themselves 
from the sports club members.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.050
Why are they jogging, anyway?

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:39.800
Who knows?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.760
Ken-chan has his own way of doing things.

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:48.000
Um—

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.520
Why did we just run like that?

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.600
You didn't like it?

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.900
That's not what I mean, I'm wondering about the reason—

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.700
Because, writing characters the normal way gets boring.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:09.040
So I thought if I started writing after running, I might 
be able to write different characters than usual.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.790
You have to motivate yourself 
for your club activities sometimes!

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:17.800
But for us, today is the first time doing club activities.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.210
Ah, that's right!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.840
Sorry!

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:25.680
Well, you two are more exhausted than 
I thought you'd be, so let's call it a day.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:29.060
It's your first day after all. You shouldn't push yourself.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.560
See you tomorrow at the clubroom!

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.980
How does one write the many characters of calligraphy~

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.730
He's so wonderful!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.700
Isn't he?

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.490
Why!?

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.460
Does this have anything to do with calligraphy?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.170
There are a lot of old writings in this house.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.300
In exchange for getting to see them, 
we're helping around the house.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.520
Granny is living alone, after all.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.880
I truly appreciate your help.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.810
She's not alone, though.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.890
Sign: Harmony

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.730
That's a nice character, isn't it?

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:21.650
It is.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:25.400
Apparently, the old lady's 
husband drew it during the war.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.200
He already passed away.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.830
I really would've liked to talk to him—

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:38.750
God?

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.420
What is it?

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.510
Er—

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.430
It's that dog!

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:50.960
What should we do?

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:53.720
I've already eaten all of my lunch!

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:54.930
Me too.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.330
God?

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.280
It's okay!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:12.830
What's up?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.450
Ah, Yurie-sama.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.660
Blah blah, thus and so, this and that.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.580
Farewell!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.000
He said you can pass.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:28.050
But he always gets startled, so he'd like you 
to pass through more quietly from now on.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.390
God are really amazing, aren't they?

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.560
That's not true!

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.390
If I confront them in earnest, I can 
understand what's on their mind!

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:27.070
<b>First Love</b>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.030
It's a lot easier to write with a roof above our head.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:34.170
But, is it really okay?

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:36.580
The ballet club might get upset—

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.860
They're out jogging right now, so it's fine.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.160
Now, let's write!

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.040
Okay!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.050
Sempai, what should I write today?

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.680
Write whatever you like.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.310
Is "friendship" okay?

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.690
If you want to write that, sure.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:07.230
Writing words you feel like writing feels 
good, and the result will end up looking great.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.860
This is no good.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:18.960
Why did you do that?

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.330
It was really well done!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:24.080
But I didn't feel very excited about it.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.460
I want to try to write some special characters.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.440
Something that goes straight 
from the heart onto the paper.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:34.590
That's what I want to write.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.550
Sign: Harmony

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:43.730
I think I understand a little.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:48.360
What kind of characters did you two 
want to write when you entered the club?

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.440
I wanted to write characters just like you do.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:57.490
I wanted to improve my handwriting—

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:00.560
I see.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:03.580
If it's about the art of writing, I can teach you.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.510
Sign: Traffic Safety

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:09.090
Sit up a little more straight, 
it'll give you more balance.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.630
Careful, if you write too small it'll get stuffy.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.760
Sign: Sea - 100 Yen

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.470
Sign: Tama

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:19.640
Try writing something.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:23.140
B-But— If I'm being stared at like that—

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.020
Nevermind me, imagine I'm not here.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:26.730
Okay.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:18:03.770
<b>Dating</b>

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.040
I'm sorry.

00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.020
Why are you apologizing?

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:58.430
They're great characters.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:03.770
Sure, they aren't drawn very 
well, but I like characters like this.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.060
Thank you!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.480
Ninomiya-sempai!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.020
Could you look at mine as well?

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:15.860
If you want to write characters just like 
me, you don't really need any advice.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.450
We're about out of paper, I'm going to fetch some more.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.210
<b>Dating</b>

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:34.210
God?

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:36.130
Y-Yes?

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:40.970
You're in love with him, aren't you?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.080
Y-You're wrong!

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.900
I'm just here to help you out!

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:51.150
Is that true? Gods really shouldn't lie!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.030
I-It's not like that—

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:16.000
Ninomiya-sempai is a strange person, isn't he?

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.550
But he's honest.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.890
That's why he can write those characters.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.390
Such wonderful characters.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.980
Sign: Sempai

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:37.900
I truly want to write characters like that as well.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:56.920
Sunrise Ferry

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:56.920
Purveyor to the god

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:46.910
Mitsue-chan?

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.210
I lied.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:55.670
Even though I'm a god.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.300
What should I do—

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:04.090
I— don't think you can do anything about it.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:10.930
I don't think that's something 
anybody can do anything about.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:17.150
So, you should probably just do 
what you feel is the best thing to do.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.740
Thanks.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.790
<b>Calligraphy 
\hClub</b>

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.790
<b>Notice of Resignation</b>

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:54.770
<b>I like you</b>

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:54.770
<b>Sempai</b>

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.430
Those are nice characters—

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:52.850
But, I'm sorry.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:54.900
<b>I like you</b>

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:54.900
<b>Sempai</b>

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:55.060
<b>I like you</b>

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:55.060
<b>Sempai</b>

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:55.190
<b>I like you</b>

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:55.190
<b>Sempai</b>

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:55.310
<b>I like you</b>

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:55.310
<b>Sempai</b>

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:55.440
<b>I like you</b>

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:55.560
<b>I like you</b>

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.280
Please accept them!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.660
You have a responsibility to accept them!

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:12.290
It's only been a very, very short time, 
but thank you for taking care of me!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:24.130
Ah— Er— Umm—

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:24.800
God?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:25.440
Yes?

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:28.220
It's your turn now!

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:44.650
<i>I can't—</i>

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:54.580
<b>Calligraphy 
\hClub</b>

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:53.200
<i>I'm still busy being a god— and a middle schooler—</i>

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:58.540
<b>I like you</b>

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:58.540
<b>Sempai</b>

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.540
I see. So you're quitting as well.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:01.340
I'm sorry—

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:03.280
It's okay.

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.020
It's merely back to how it was now.

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:07.050
I'm content with being on my own.

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:11.400
If you ever feel up to it again, give me a holler.

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:24.320
Okay.

00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:33.950
As I was saying, despite it being summer vacation, 
it doesn't mean you can merrily play around.

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:38.290
Exactly because it is a long vacation, it is 
a great opportunity to learn many things.

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:43.040
It is to further climb the stairs of adulthood, step by step.

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:43.710
Please—

00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:48.720
What are we going to do over summer vacation?

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:50.750
Let's see—

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:54.180
Special training, business, there are a lot of things to do.

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:57.680
But let's start off by playing around!

00:22:58.690 --> 00:22:59.940
It's summer after all.

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:05.110
In favor.

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:16.370
Thanks, Mitsue-chan, Matsuri-chan.

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:27.310
<b>mada mada zenzen owannai last ichijikan no jugyou desu</b>

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:27.310
<b>The last class of the day never seems to end</b>

00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:32.200
<b>tokei wo chira chira mitemo ichi byou ga nagai ne</b>

00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:32.200
<b>Even if I keep glancing at my watch, a second seems an eternity</b>

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:39.260
<b>mabushii koutei mieru kimi no hashiru sugata oikake</b>

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:39.260
<b>In the radiant schoolyard, trailing your running visage,</b>

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:44.390
<b>houkago love-love date mousou shite bosou chuu</b>

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:44.390
<b>my imagination is running wild about our date after class</b>

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:48.310
<b>chime no kane koi no signal</b>

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:48.310
<b>The school chimes ring and it's a signal of love!</b>

00:23:48.310 --> 00:23:51.280
<b>rouka no tobidashi ni wa chuui</b>

00:23:48.310 --> 00:23:51.280
<b>Be careful if you rush out into the hallway!</b>

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>kimi no moto e ichiban saki ni</b>

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>I dash to see you, first thing!</b>

00:23:54.250 --> 00:23:56.890
<b>issho ni kaerou</b>

00:23:54.250 --> 00:23:56.890
<b>Let's go home together!</b>

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:04.510
<b>soda aji no ice candy gira gira na ohisama no shita hanbunko</b>

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:04.510
<b>Sharing a soda-flavored popsicle under the glaring sun</b>

00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:10.570
<b>torokesou na atashi no seishun desu doki doki shichau</b>

00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:10.570
<b>My youth seems to melt with it, it makes my heart beat faster</b>

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:16.040
<b>kono nanigenai toki wo ima mune ni shimatte</b>

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:16.040
<b>I'm shutting our casual time in my heart</b>

00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:23.470
<b>asu wa mata kyou yori mo kimi wo suki ni naru no desu</b>

00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:23.470
<b>Tomorrow I will love you even more than today</b>

00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:42.620
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:30.550
The shining sun, the azure skies—

00:24:31.020 --> 00:24:35.730
I will rekindle the memories of a forgotten beach.

00:24:36.450 --> 00:24:38.660
Next time, Lovers of the Sun.

00:24:37.530 --> 00:24:42.620
<b>Lovers of the Sun</b>

00:24:39.170 --> 00:24:41.000
It'll be settled by a chu!
